      "summary": "Gift Card – Checkout: Multiple Gift Cards, Sole Payment & Split Payment Logic",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want to apply one or more gift cards or credit notes at checkout and combine them with other payment methods if needed, so that I can use my available balances flexibly.\\n\\nThis story covers all gift card and credit note payment combination logic at checkout: sole payment — gift card or credit note covers the full order total via a single GiveX call (GC-044); split payment with card/PayPal/Apple Pay — gift card balance applied first, remaining balance charged to the secondary method (GC-045); gift card and credit note combined together (GC-046); combined with Retail Rewards vouchers (GC-047); combined with promotional codes (GC-048); multiple gift cards or credit notes applied in a single transaction — the system allows more than one card per order, open question on maximum number (GC-049 — @Jasmijn Tsang to confirm max); gift card and credit note redemption is not supported on Global-e international storefronts (GC-050). GiveX side of all transactions is owned by this epic — Adyen side is owned by SFCC-381 (Split Payment UI) and SFCC-382 (Split Payment backend). Surface: SFCC/PWA Kit checkout payment logic. Owned by: SFCC/PWA Kit.\\n\\nNote: this story sits correctly in SFCC-17 (Credit Notes & Gift Cards). Open item: confirm maximum number of gift cards per transaction with Jasmijn Tsang.\\n\\nDepends on GC-044–GC-050. Cross-epic dependency: SFCC-78 (GiveX), SFCC-381, SFCC-382 (Payments split payment stories), SFCC-87 (Promotions/Retail Rewards).",
