    },
    {
      "id": "17865",
      "key": "SFCC-32",
      "summary": "Feedonomics Product Feed",
      "description": "As a\n digital marketing team,\nI want\n SFCC to export scheduled product catalogue feeds to Feedonomics,\nso that\n marketing channels have accurate, up-to-date product data to power paid and organic campaigns.\nFunctional Requirements Overview\nReq ID\nRequirement\nPRD-071\nThe system should support product catalogue feed provision through our existing feeds provider, Feedonomics. It should be possible to restrict the volume of product fed into Feedonomics at import rather than once the import is on the Feedonomics servers. The feeds should support product availability, stock positions, pricing, visibility, labels, and other metadata.\nPRD-017\nThe system should ensure all product states (Coming Soon, Back in Soon, Unavailable) comply with Google Merchant Centre feed rules; products in ineligible states should not surface in product feeds.\nINT-*\nThe system will run scheduled SFCC Business Manager jobs to export product catalogue feeds to Feedonomics including product availability, stock positions, pricing, visibility, labels and metadata. Feed configuration, product feed management and Google Merchant Centre setup are out of scope for SFCC and remain with Zimmermann. \n(Source: 04.1.17 Third Party Integrations)\nBackground\nSFCC is the system of record for product catalogue data. Feedonomics is the downstream feed management platform responsible for distributing product data to external marketing channels. SFCC's responsibility is limited to generating and exporting well-formed, complete feeds on a scheduled basis. Feed configuration, product feed management and Google Merchant Centre setup are out of scope for SFCC and remain with Zimmermann.\nScope\nSFCC will run scheduled Business Manager jobs to export product catalogue feeds to Feedonomics. Each feed is storefront-specific, reflecting that storefront's product availability, stock positions, pricing, visibility, labels and metadata. Feeds will be exported for all active storefronts: AU, US, UK, EU Domestic, EU International, ME and HK.\nThe volume of products included in the feed is configurable at the job level — restriction can be applied at export rather than post-import in Feedonomics.\nOut of Scope\nFeed configuration and optimisation within Feedonomics\nGoogle Merchant Centre setup and management\nMarketing channel mapping or distribution logic\nAny downstream consumers of Feedonomics data",
